WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.760
I wish I never found out
about love.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:10.730
I love you.
My tears won't stop.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.830
<i>Everyone is supporting me.</i>

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:18.030
- If this is how it's going to be,
<i>- Everyone is making me shine.</i>

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.800
- I wish I had
<i>- So I'll continue to sing.</i>

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.600
- never met you.
<i>- Just like the moon that waxes</i>

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>and shines even</i>
<i>after it wanes.</i>

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.000
Good morning, Eichi.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.330
Please watch over me from
up in the sky again today!

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.030
Takuto! Meroko!

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:26.260
Good morning!

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:27.160
Hi!

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:27.860
Good morning!

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.260
Hey, you!

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.260
At least wear a pair of socks
when it's this cold!

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.160
Do you want to be hospitalized
again or something?

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.160
Okay!

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.000
Mitsuki! Breakfast!

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:44.030
Okay!

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:04.230
Mitsuki...

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:04.930
Yes?

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:09.160
Well...
How is school?

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.700
We've recently started
practicing for graduation.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.130
I see.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.330
<i>Ma'am...</i>

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.100
What do you think
about them?

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.930
Seems to me they aren't
quite meshing right.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:25.800
Yeah.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.760
W-Well, I guess it'll
still take some time.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.060
What do you mean
"ah ha ha"?

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.200
Is it still bothering you?

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.730
W-What are
you talking about?

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:48.360
I'm not bothered by
anything in the least!

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:03.530
Hey, I've told you numerous times
that I don't think you're at fault.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:04.700
But...

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:05.800
No "buts"!

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:09.730
I told you before, the whole thing
is Izumi's fault, right?!

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:11.360
Yeah.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:14.660
Gimme a break. How long are
you gonna mope like that?

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.000
Don't make me
worry anymore.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.630
Takuto! Thank you!

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.200
Idiot! Stop that!

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:38.430
Mitsuki...

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:40.030
Yes?

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.560
Umm... About your room...

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:44.700
Yes?

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:49.160
W-Why don't you move
into the main house?

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.160
Huh?

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.200
<i>Ma'am!</i>

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.130
It's inconvenient where
you are now, isn't it?

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.460
And we have to think
about your health.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:01.700
Grandma...

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.360
Please move into
the main house.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:08.200
Okay!

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.060
Yay!

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:15.130
Good morning!

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.160
Thank you for helping out
every morning.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.300
No problem.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:23.030
Grandma, Ms. Tanaka,
I'll see you later.

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:24.700
Take care.

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:27.800
Thank you for helping
Mitsuki again today.

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:30.100
Sure thing!
Well, shall we go.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:31.130
Okay!

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:33.930
See you later!

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.930
Have a good day!

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:43.730
Come, Ma'am.
It's cold out here, so let's go inside.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.060
Yes.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.060
Huh? Work?

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:50.100
Yeah.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:54.560
Given what happened,
and considering your health,

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:58.530
I told the office to turn down
work whenever possible.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:00.200
But just today...

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.860
It's no problem at all, Ms. Oshige!

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:10.060
This is my first job since my recovery!
I'll do my best!

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:13.060
<i>Thank you, Mitsuki.</i>

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:20.800
See you later!

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:22.960
I'll come pick you up later!

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.130
Okay!

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:46.330
So, greetings from
the honored guests finish here

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:48.800
and then the diplomas
will be handed out.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.660
- Did you watch Yaba last night?
- We'll start with the boys from Class 1

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.100
- Yeah, yeah!
- lining up by the stairs

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:54.800
- It was really funny!
- and then three people will

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:55.900
- Did you see it, Mitsuki?
- come up on stage at a time.

00:06:56.130 --> 00:06:56.800
Yeah.

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:59.100
Hey! You!
Stop the chitchat!

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:00.860
Oops.

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:11.300
Takuto...

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.200
Please!

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:13.160
Okay.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:42.960
All right, shall we go?

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:43.960
Okay!

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:53.430
Good morning!

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:55.030
- Good morning!
- Good morning!

00:07:58.400 --> 00:07:59.830
Dr. Wakaoji...

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:01.060
Hi!

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:03.130
What are you doing here?

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:05.530
I heard you were working
again starting today.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:09.760
I asked Keichi to be here
in case of emergency.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.460
It's not only that.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.400
I wanted to hear you
sing in person, Mitsuki.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:17.560
If you don't feel well,
let me know immediately.

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.000
Yes!

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:36.360
<i>How long has it been</i>
<i>since I fell in love with you?</i>

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:45.430
<i>My feelings keep</i>
<i>getting stronger.</i>

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:54.530
<i>They're silent like the snow.</i>

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.200
<i>What did you say?</i>

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:05.160
<i>U-Unbelievable.</i>
<i>No way.</i>

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:08.930
<i>Are you...</i>
<i>Are you really...</i>

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.360
<i>Yes, I'm Takuto Kira.</i>

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:14.330
<i>That's a lie.</i>
<i>I don't believe you!</i>

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:17.630
<i>I can't believe...</i>
<i>I can't believe that Takuto died!</i>

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:19.360
<i>Keichi...</i>

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.460
<i>But how do you explain</i>
<i>the way you look?</i>

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:23.860
<i>What about your voice?!</i>

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.600
<i>The Takuto I know is</i>
<i>a totally different person!</i>

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:33.960
<i>First of all, why wasn't I</i>
<i>aware of it before now?</i>

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.460
<i>I see.</i>

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:44.300
<i>So that's what happened to you</i>
<i>after Route L broke up.</i>

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:45.630
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:48.800
<i>I apologize for getting</i>
<i>all worked up like that earlier.</i>

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:49.860
<i>It's okay.</i>

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:53.130
<i>But it still doesn't</i>
<i>sit right with me.</i>

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:55.260
<i>But I've explained</i>
<i>everything to you!</i>

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.000
<i>No, it's not that.</i>

00:09:57.460 --> 00:10:00.730
<i>It doesn't sit right because we were</i>
<i>such close friends back then.</i>

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:01.600
<i>Huh?</i>

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:06.960
<i>Why... Why are you a Death Spirit</i>
<i>who is trying to take Mitsuki's life?</i>

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:10.500
<i>It can't be helped.</i>

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:16.060
<i>I don't want to do this either. But...</i>

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:24.460
<i>If the snow falls forever,</i>

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.660
<i>will I be able to let go</i>
<i>of these thoughts of you?</i>

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:28.500
Hey.

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:31.130
About what we were speaking
about the other day...

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:32.430
Yeah?

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.930
Sorry to tell you this,
Death Spirit,

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:38.330
but I have no intention
of letting Mitsuki die.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:42.760
If the cause of Mitsuki's death
is her throat illness,

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:45.130
I, as her doctor,
will root it out.

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:46.960
That is my mission.

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:51.330
It is true that I am a Death Spirit.
But...

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.360
I don't have any intention
of letting that girl die.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:56.830
Takuto.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.600
Our objectives are the same.

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:05.660
<i>I want to scream in</i>
<i>the winter sky</i>

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:07.760
I look forward to
working with you!

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:16.060
<i>that I want to</i>
<i>see you right now.</i>

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:41.960
Wow, it was so much fun
to work after such a long time!

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:46.130
You're not overdoing it, are you?
Are you feeling all right?

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:47.360
I'm totally fine.

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:49.000
I see. That's a relief.

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:52.600
Ms. Oshige!
Please stop right here!

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:00.930
What? I don't need to
drop you off at home?

00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:02.130
No.

00:12:03.560 --> 00:12:06.330
Well then, Ms. Oshige,
thank you very much!

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:07.860
You're welcome.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:11.860
Everyone!

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:12.930
Oh, Mitsuki!

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:14.360
Good evening!

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.530
Did you just get back
from your check-up?

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.330
Well then, please take
good care of Mitsuki.

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:20.700
- Yeah.
- Okay.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:27.400
So cool...

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:28.930
She's been driving you around

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:30.860
ever since you were released
from the hospital, hasn't she?

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:32.430
Wow.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:36.960
But is it really okay for a racecar
to drive on ordinary streets?

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:43.560
I feel like it's really starting to
hit me that we're graduating soon.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:47.200
But even after we graduate, we'll still
see each other at the same junior high.

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:48.460
Right, Mitsuki?!

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:50.400
Y-Yeah!

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:52.930
Graduating all together, huh?

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.500
I hope that we'll all be
in the same class again.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:01.230
Yeah, that would be great!

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:02.930
Wouldn't it?

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.900
You say that...

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:08.730
But you want to be in the same class
with Machida, don't you, Kumi?

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.330
W-What are you
talking about?

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:12.430
Oh, you're blushing!

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:14.230
Stop that, Wakana!

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:17.330
I'm jealous!
I want a boyfriend!

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:18.830
Shut it!

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:20.760
I want one too!

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:27.130
- See you!
- See you!

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:28.500
Okay, see you at school!

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:29.630
- Bye!
- Bye!

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:30.660
See you tomorrow!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:31.700
See ya!

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:39.430
I lied.

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:41.100
What about?

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:45.360
That I would be going to the same
junior high school as everyone.

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:47.030
Mitsuki...

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:51.230
I won't be able to go
to junior high, will I?

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:56.660
But it's all right.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:01.560
Until then, I will give my all in my singing,
and I'll live with all my might.

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:04.500
I'm sure Eichi would
want that too.

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:07.130
So that's why you're
saying it's all right?

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:08.100
Yeah!

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:10.600
So you're gonna lie
to me too?

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:12.000
Huh?

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.530
Please be honest with me.

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:16.760
I am being honest—

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:17.460
That's not true!

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:21.430
If you want to live,
say you want to live!

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:24.330
If you're scared,
say you're scared!

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:27.700
Don't lie to me.

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:31.500
It's natural to feel that way.

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:34.830
Don't hold it all within yourself.

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:37.500
In that case...

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:43.360
So if I were to say that,
is that gonna change something?

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:48.900
That I want to live, or that I'm scared...
Is that gonna change something?

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:51.930
To tell the truth...

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:54.430
To tell the truth, I really...

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:04.800
It'll be all right. Don't worry.

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:06.560
I won't let you die.

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:13.360
I won't lie to you either.
I will protect you.

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:16.260
I won't let you die
no matter what.

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:22.400
<i>The only person who can</i>
<i>protect her now is me.</i>

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.560
<i>That's right.</i>
<i>This is the best way.</i>

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:53.560
<i>Betraying someone you love and</i>
<i>seeking happiness just for yourself...</i>

00:15:55.630 --> 00:15:58.000
<i>I'm the worst.</i>

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:11.160
So you finally understood?
Whatever will be, will be.

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.630
We should be together too.

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:17.130
Who would want that?!

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:23.230
You're very defiant, aren't you, Mero?
But this is the last chance.

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:27.700
Now... Come back to me.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:36.230
You're mistaken.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:41.700
What I felt as I watched
the two of them

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:45.800
was that loving someone is
something much more tranquil.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:48.130
Takuto forgave me.

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:53.000
He forgave the person
who betrayed him and

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:56.400
was the very cause of
his possibly becoming a ghost.

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:02.960
And also, despite putting himself
in potentially dangerous situations,

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:05.300
he always protected that girl.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:10.860
I believe that loving someone means
having that kind of tranquil big heart.

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:14.400
What are you saying, Mero?

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:21.430
In that way... In an even bigger way...
I do love Takuto after all.

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:28.500
Why? A guy like Takuto who can't
even do his work as a Death Spirit?

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:29.830
That's exactly why.

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:33.200
Because he has a much more
beautiful heart than we do.

00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:38.900
He doesn't have to be able to do the work
of a Death Spirit who just reaps lives.

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:44.960
I love Takuto as a person.

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:47.800
Mero...

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:51.500
You probably don't
understand, do you?

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:55.160
That's your misfortune, Izumi.

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:57.560
My misfortune?

00:17:59.860 --> 00:18:00.530
Goodbye!

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:19.330
I wonder where Meroko went.

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.200
Jeez...

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:24.360
That idiot.

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:34.060
Huh? Umm...

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:35.100
Meroko!

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.730
Takuto, who are you
calling an idiot?

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:39.730
Jeez, where were you?

00:18:39.900 --> 00:18:41.530
We were worried about you!

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:45.330
Both of you are really kind,
aren't you?

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:50.160
I love both of you!

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:55.960
M-Meroko, what's the matter,
saying things like that out of the blue?

00:18:57.330 --> 00:19:00.360
Huh? Nothing!

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:02.630
Th-That hurts!
Get away from me!

00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:06.300
Then, just Mitsuki...

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:08.700
That feels so warm!

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:13.400
Mitsuki! Dinner!

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:14.660
Okay!

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:22.960
Grandma?

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:24.960
What is it?

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:30.030
Your suggestion to move
into the main house... Umm...

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:33.830
Could you wait
just a little longer?

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:35.060
Huh?

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:35.760
Huh?

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:39.200
Umm... It's not that I don't want to move,
and there's no deep meaning behind it!

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:40.930
I guess I could say
I first need closure.

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:42.730
Or how could I put it?

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:46.600
Ma'am...

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:49.400
I see.

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:53.000
If it's a decision
you have made, Mitsuki.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:56.130
I understand.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:19:59.660
Grandma, thank you!

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:03.360
Don't worry about it.
I look forward to you moving in.

00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:05.060
Ma'am...

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:07.430
Come, finish up.

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:08.330
Okay!

00:20:10.130 --> 00:20:12.860
<i>I'd like the three of us,</i>
<i>Takuto, Meroko and I,</i>

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:15.060
<i>to be together in that annex</i>
<i>just a little longer.</i>

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:17.360
<i>I'm sorry, Grandma.</i>

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:20.630
Hey, Meroko.

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:21.500
What?

00:20:22.130 --> 00:20:24.200
You said that a keyword
hasn't appeared

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:26.160
since Eichi's backwards name
disappeared, right?

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:27.900
Huh? Yeah. Why?

00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:30.530
Could you lend me the Death Spirit
Handbook for a moment?

00:20:30.960 --> 00:20:32.730
What's up all of a sudden?

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:36.800
Here.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:39.060
Okay then.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:42.330
Huh?

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:43.760
TAKUTO KIRA
I am the keyword.

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:46.800
W-What are you doing?!

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:51.800
Takuto! Do you understand
what this means?

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:53.200
Of course.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:54.330
Then why?!

00:20:55.700 --> 00:20:58.260
What the heck is fate anyway?
It's stupid.

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:04.030
If no one is able to change
that girl's fate, I will change it.

00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:06.800
Takuto...

00:21:11.560 --> 00:21:13.530
There's no way
a half-baked guy like you

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:15.730
could do something
like that alone!

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:18.560
Meroko! You...

00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:20.930
Yeah!

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:22.330
TAKUTO KIRA
MEROKO YUI
Me too.

00:23:06.600 --> 00:23:07.600
What happened?

00:23:07.630 --> 00:23:09.530
She relapsed from
her transformation all of a sudden

00:23:09.560 --> 00:23:11.130
back into her
12-year-old self!

00:23:11.330 --> 00:23:13.430
My Death Spirit powers are
just a little weak right now.

00:23:13.460 --> 00:23:14.630
Don't worry about it.

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:16.560
Takuto, could that mean...

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:19.630
It's fine.
Do you not trust me?

00:23:19.860 --> 00:23:20.530
But...

00:23:21.130 --> 00:23:24.400
I decided that I would help her
achieve her dream in one year.

00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:26.230
I'm keeping my promise!

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:30.760
Next time on Full Moon:
"I Can't Be Full Moon."

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:32.330
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
